      "id": "erdos-243",
      "title": "Erdős #243: Cubic-rate irrationality and reciprocal tails",
      "authors": [
        "Will Cook"
      ],
      "href": "https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/a501de956765730ba4e6c9ad284e6d65855d533a/paper/243/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.pdf",
      "here": false,
      "sentence": "I prove that a strictly increasing integer sequence with a_n²/a_(n+1) = 1 + 3/n + o(n⁻³) has an irrational sum of reciprocals. I also prove the result for every nonintegral regular rate above one. Lean checks both results. The unrestricted Sylvester-tail question remains open.",
